                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e6a20792-3e01-3aac-89e8-1e13051f6d69",
                        "entry_id": "c2e3925b-11f8-37fb-944a-5c219b9c78c1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "flowing with milk"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f1cbc53b-7208-4d81-bc48-296fc397de12",
                                "sense_id": "e6a20792-3e01-3aac-89e8-1e13051f6d69",
                                "text": "Me. But how does that appear? Og. Oh, the nun at Constantinople that gave it said so. Me. It may be she had it of St. Bernard. Og. I believe she had. Me. He, when he was very old, had the happiness to taste milk from the same nipple which the child Jesus sucked, whence I wonder he was not rather called Lactifluous than Mellifluous."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "de9ac2c6-7ae3-4cd8-ba3d-d64e3e321b05",
                                "sense_id": "e6a20792-3e01-3aac-89e8-1e13051f6d69",
                                "text": "But the pronouncing aright of California names is only a part of the duty. There needs to be a present crusade for the preservation of our historical names from oblivion.¶ It is not so much the lactifluous tenderfoot who is our danger in this case, but the wax-witted Philistines of the Post Office Department and the railroads; two Boeotian despots that have a great deal to do with place names and who have committed some of the most cold-blooded murders known to etymology."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "82800bab-22e1-4f7f-a801-478ffb61fbe1",
                                "sense_id": "e6a20792-3e01-3aac-89e8-1e13051f6d69",
                                "text": "On March 1 a bleary-eyed, drop-horned and also knock-kneed 9-year-old Friesian cow named Bridge Birch (above) of Moortown Farm, Hampshire, England, concluded a lactifluous year by producing her 45,081st pound of milk."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "480229a3-531d-4268-9d67-e810daf61a7c",
                                "sense_id": "e6a20792-3e01-3aac-89e8-1e13051f6d69",
                                "text": "The bare teats of the human females bored out from this two-dimensional undergrowth like the barrels of lactifluous guns."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
